    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557-a2">

                <pb facs="0620" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg540"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinolosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Satow to Mr. Bergholz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Van</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-05-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 12,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that an
                    American citizen, Dr. C. D. Ussher, of the American mission, has been summoned
                    to appear before the Istintak court of this town on a criminal charge.</p>
                <p>The facts of the case are as follows: Last summer a corporal of Hamidieh Cavalry,
                    by name Tahir, son of Aziz, resident in the village of Rikava, in the Norduz
                    Nahieh <pb facs="0621" n="541" xml:id="pg541"/> of the Shattak Kaza of this
                    vilayet, was brought to Dr. Ussher for treatment. He was suffering from an
                    affliction of the brain, caused by a blow from a stone. The operation of
                    trepanning was successfully performed, and all would have gone well had he not
                    persisted in thrusting his hand underneath the bandages. This caused suppuration
                    and death resulted. The charge of hastening the natural causes of death which
                    has been brought by the relatives of the deceased is entirely without
                    foundation, and is, I fancy, made at the instigation of the former municipal
                    doctor, Fathe Bey, who has now left this town. He was no friend of Dr. Ussher
                    and wished to place difficulties in his way.</p>
                <p>I have informed the local authorities that the case must be referred to the
                    Sublime Porte, and have also notified His Majesty’s embassy for the information
                    of the United States legation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. E. Satow</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">His Britannic Majesty’s Acting
                        Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
